How to read it: `requiredProps` / `optionalProps` are the ONLY props a component accepts, `variants`
lists the allowed literal values, and `prop_shapes` gives the member names INSIDE object props —
`"CredentialStrip.items[]": "title, detail"` means every element of `items` is `{ title, detail }`,
and `?` marks an optional member. These names are read from the component sources; they are exact.

=== PROP CONTRACT (highest-value rule on this page) ===
A wrong prop name does not fail the build — it renders an EMPTY component. `CredentialStrip` given
`{ label, value }` instead of `{ title, detail }` paints four blank cards under a live heading.
- Pass EXACTLY the documented prop names and EXACTLY the documented member names. Never rename,
  never add a member the shape does not list, never guess a shape that is not in `prop_shapes`.
- Pass every required prop and never omit a required prop — `MarketingHero` without `imageSrc`
  does not compile.
- Never invent a prop: no `target` on `Button`, no `children` on `MarketingHero`, no `name` on an
  `ActivityFeed` item. If a prop is not in `requiredProps`/`optionalProps`, it does not exist.
- Literal props take only the listed values — `variant="default"` is wrong where the contract says
  `'primary' | 'secondary'`.
- Only read `seed.*` / `images.*` keys that `@/data/mock` actually exports. `images` has exactly
  `hero`, `hero2`, `card1`, `card2`, `card3`, `ambient` — no other image key exists.
- An empty array is a blank section. Every list prop gets real business items.

=== LEGIBILITY ===
Catalogue components manage their own contrast over their own imagery — trust the design tokens.
- Never put background, overlay, blend or opacity utilities in a catalogue component's `className`:
  no `bg-background`, `bg-*`, `after:bg-*`, `bg-blend-*`, `mix-blend-*`, `opacity-*`. A generated
  page added `after:bg-blend-multiply after:bg-text-brand/20 bg-background` to `MarketingHero` and
  turned the headline, subcopy and secondary CTA white-on-white.
- `className` on catalogue components is for spacing and width only (`mt-*`, `py-*`, `max-w-*`).

